1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,290
Alice loads her dashboard: "Welcome back, Alice".

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:11,990
Bob loads the same page and sees "Welcome back, Alice".

3
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:19,630
Bob's response: Alice's name, Alice's email, same render number.

4
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:27,270
A deliberately flawed application cache, not a CDN incident.

5
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:34,840
The cache key is the path only: /dashboard.

6
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:39,570
Two identities, one shared slot.

7
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:46,800
Authentication was correct. The cached payload was not.

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:54,040
Cache-Control does not repair code that ignores it.

9
00:00:54,040 --> 00:01:01,140
Bypass the shared slot. Authenticate and authorise every request.

10
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:06,660
Send private, no-store. Purge the old entry.

11
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:14,210
Two independent cookie jars. Alice, Bob, Alice, Bob.

12
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:19,880
The shared slot is never touched.

13
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:27,750
Each user receives only their own page.

14
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:33,370
Already-delivered responses cannot be retracted.

15
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:37,590
A cache key defines which requests you treat as equivalent.
